//!
//! # Fs
//!
//! Files: the initramfs archive the kernel boots with.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name            | File            | Purpose                                         |
//! |-----------------|-----------------|-------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Fs::Tar`       | `tar.ign`       | reads the members of a ustar archive, checked   |
//! | `Fs::Initramfs` | `initramfs.ign` | finds the initramfs module and validates it     |
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! | Imports   | Why                                              |
//! |-----------|--------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Mm`      | the initramfs is a Limine module                 |
//! | `Lib`     | `memcpy` and `memmove` for paths                 |
//! | `Drivers` | the boot report                                  |
//!
//! `Fs` sits above `Mm` and below `Proc`: a process opens files, and the
//! files need memory.

import _ from "./initramfs";
import _ from "./tar";

/// Aggregate namespace of the file code. The files above contribute the
/// sub-namespaces listed in the module header.
export namespace Fs {}
